 (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Comstock Resources, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.9B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -15% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $450M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 73% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (32.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are u